{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Therefore the well was called 'the well of the living One who sees me' (באר לחי ראי).</b> From the language of (1 Samuel 25:6) כה לחי — 'thus to life'; that is to say, a well of the other year, when he would be alive he would see me. And the reason is that every year the Ishmaelites would make festival at this well; even today it is called 'the well of Zamzam.' End of quotation."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:45.677688547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}